=== Prompt ===
Who is Pikachu?

=== Normal Response ===
Pikachu is a fictional creature from the popular media franchise Pokémon. It is a small, rodent-like Pokémon with electric powers. Pikachu is one of the most well-known and beloved Pokémon, and it is often considered the mascot of the franchise.

Pikachu is a Electric-type Pokémon, which means it has the ability to generate and store electricity in its cheeks, which it can use to attack its opponents. It is known for its bright yellow color, red cheeks, and its ability to store electricity in its cheeks, which it can release in the form of powerful electric attacks.

Pikachu is a popular character in the Pokémon franchise, and it has appeared in numerous Pokémon games, anime episodes, movies, and other media. It is often depicted as the partner of the main character, Ash Ketchum, in the Pokémon anime series.

Pikachu has become a cultural icon and a symbol of the Pokémon franchise, and it is widely recognized around the world. It has been featured in various forms of media, including video games, anime, manga, and merchandise.

Pikachu's popularity can be attributed to its cute and endearing appearance, its unique abilities, and its role as a loyal and trusted partner to Ash Ketchum. It has become a beloved character in popular culture, and it continues to be a popular and iconic character in the Pokémon franchise.

